-814 CE). This era marked a resurgence of art, culture, and learning in Western Europe, with Aachen serving as the capital of the Carolingian Empire and a site of significant political power. The city's palatine chapel, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, exemplifies the architectural innovation of the time and reflects the synthesis of classical and Christian elements, making Aachen an enduring symbol of medieval Europe.

